    {
      "id": "5691444f-b168-4760-a7c6-9819a8cf4bd8",
      "title": "Lemma 3 — inserting the small pieces costs at most max(A, (1+g) OPT(I) + 1) bins",
      "milestone_description": "Lemma 3  Let $I$ be an instance of the bin-packing problem, and let $g$ be a real number between 0 and 1. Designate each piece as *large* if its size is $> \\frac{g}{2}$ and *small* otherwise. Consider a process which starts with a given packing of the large pieces into bins, and then inserts the small pieces, starting a new bin only when necessary. If the cost of the given packing of the large pieces is $A$, then the cost of the packing resulting from the process is $\\le max(A, (1+g)\\,OPT(I) + 1)$ .\n",
      "sort_order": 2,
      "completed": true,
      "theorem": {
        "id": "2ff92ced-97ae-493b-98aa-8a7700b97db2",
        "theorem_name": "KKBinPacking.GeometricGrouping.anyFit_card_le",
        "status": "Proved"
